{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And YHWH Elohim formed from the ground every beast of the field.</b> He gave them the perfection of sensible form, for which the celestial force alone was not sufficient at that time without a generative power to assist it." "<b>And He brought to the man.</b> In order that he might recognize that a new being needed to be brought into existence, since among the animals there was nothing fit to serve him." "<b>To see what he would call it.</b> So that he might see and discern what name is proper for each one of them according to the activity specific to its form." "<b>Living soul is its name.</b> Its name indicates the form of the animal called by that name — namely, the soul through which it exists in actuality."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:28:42.275454386Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}